notesT: The big one this build: the camera pulse should actually LOCK now.
  rPPG FIX (from your device log): your finger was on the lens the whole time, but the
  red level drifted across the finger-detection threshold every ~8 s, so the app kept
  flipping "finger yes/no". Each "no" wiped the heart-rate estimate and left gaps in the
  pulse signal, so it never locked (bpm stuck at 0, confidence never climbed). The
  finger-detection now has hysteresis — once your finger is detected it HOLDS through the
  dips instead of dropping out, so the signal stays continuous and the pulse can lock.
  Test 10.79.2: Bio page → cover the rear camera + flash, hold still ~15–20 s → you should
  get a stable BPM with confidence climbing (not flickering back to "—"). If the red level
  still reads very low on your device, tell me and I'll raise the torch brightness next.
  ALSO carries 10.79.1's polish: Breathing only on the Bio page, ≥44pt tap targets on
  Mute/Solo · Share · Browser star · Arrange controls, consistent theme colours.
